  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc while image-only (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We have only one RNA data point and don't know whether multiprofile aggregation (vs singleprofile) meaningfully improves the RNA signal. This experiment (config_002) tests multiprofile + avgpool with the same pca_n2000 encoder, providing the cleanest isolated comparison to config_001 by changing only the profile setting and adding a simple aggregation. It is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) it directly extends our strongest configuration, (2) it resolves whether the profile/aggregation axis matters for the dominant modality before we invest in more complex encoders or multimodal fusion, and (3) the result will inform whether multiprofile is worth pursuing in any multimodal setup, reducing uncertainty across a large portion of the remaining search space."
}

